From bd9b35c3afc929c3686a3ed40506f3f4d32cab1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartheek Nagasuri <kartheek@artiumacademy.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:47:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat: allow parent work items from other projects in the
 same workspace

Backend
- Parent validation (app, draft and public API serializers) now checks the
  parent is in the same workspace instead of the same project, requires the
  acting user to be a non-guest member of the parent's project when it is in
  another project, and rejects cycles. Shared helper in plane/utils/issue_parent.py.
- Sub work items GET returns only children from projects the user is a
  member of; POST scopes the parent to the workspace/project, excludes the
  parent and its ancestors, and logs activity under each sub work item's own
  project with the correct previous parent.
- Parent search excludes all descendants (not just direct children) and no
  longer crashes when the issue has no parent.

Frontend
- Parent picker and "add existing sub work item" modal gain the workspace
  level toggle.
- Sub work items are fetched under the parent's own project.
- parent_id is preserved when switching project in the create modal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
